15. Qe2 Ne4 16. O-O Nxg3 17. fxg3 O-O 18. b4 d4 19. Kh1 dxe3 20. Qxe3 Qxe3 21.
Bxe3 Rc3 22. Rbd1 Bg4 23. Rd2 Rxa3 24. Bc5 Bxc5 25. bxc5 g6 26. Be4 Rb3 27. Bd5
Rb5 28. h3 Be6 29. Bxe6 fxe6 30. Rxf8+ Kxf8 31. Rd7 a5 32. Rxh7 Kg8 {? EMJ} 33.
Re7 e5 34. Rxe5 Kf7 35. Rd5 a4 36. Rd4 Ra5 37. Rd7+ Ke8 38. Rxb7 a3 39. Rb1 a2
40. Ra1 Kd7 41. h4 Kc6 42. g4 Kxc5 43. h5 gxh5 44. gxh5 Kb4 {Then, no move for
White, but what looks like "K-N6" [45...Kb3] is written, followed by "Resigns".
Sources: Andrew Stone, great-grandson of EM Jellie; image of this game score
at the Streatham & Brixton blog: http://streathambrixtonchess.blogspot.com/
2014/12/county-counting-5-in-jellie-mould.html - it is not absolutely certain
that the game was played at the 1935/36 Hastings but it seems probable.} (44...
Kb4 45. g4 {or 45 Kh2 would lead to a draw with best play, so perhaps White
blundered with 45 Kg1, followed by resignation after 45...Kb3.}) 0-1

